{
    "background_story": "Jadiel grew up with a baseball in his hand and a dream in his heart. As a young boy, he would spend hours playing catch with his father in the backyard, imagining himself as a pro player. Years later, Jadiel's talent and dedication earned him a spot on his college team. After a successful collegiate career, he was drafted into the minor leagues. Jadiel's hard work and perseverance eventually paid off, and he made his major league debut at the iconic Wrigley Field. The roar of the crowd, the smell of hot dogs, and the crack of the bat as he stepped up to the plate - it was a moment he had envisioned countless times in the ballpark of his childhood. Jadiel's journey was a testament to the power of chasing one's dreams, no matter how big or daunting they may seem.",
